{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cibophobic-moist-guineafowl","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nThe rebar MCP server on the box writes ticket events into a clone whose `tickets` branch cannot\npush to `origin/tickets`. Every write through the MCP tracker surface — comments, edits,\n`set_file_impact`, links, transitions — is committed locally in that container and **never\nreaches the shared store**. The tool call returns success.\n\nAny agent following AGENTS.md's mandate to 'route tracker ops through the MCP server' is therefore\nwriting to a store nobody else can see, including the gates, which read the CLI-side store.\n\n## Observed independently by three agents this session\n\n- `push_status: final-push-rejected` (\"fetch first\") on every MCP write.\n- The unpushed count CLIMBS across calls, so it is not a transient losing one race:\n  50 -> 69 in one session, 56 -> 63 in another, and `fsck` on the container reported the local\n  `tickets` branch **84 commits ahead** of `origin/tickets`.\n- Two agents independently found their MCP-written `set_file_impact` and comments stranded, and\n  had to re-issue them through the local CLI store before the gates could see them.\n\n## Why the local CLI store is healthy and this one is not\n\nThe developer-side store reconciles a non-fast-forward by MERGING `origin/tickets`\n(`src/rebar/_store/push.py:7-9` — merge, never rebase). That path demonstrably works: the local\nstore went from 141 unpushed to 0 without intervention during this session. The container's store\nis not recovering the same way, so either that recovery path is not running there, or it is\nrunning and failing for a reason the CLI store does not hit.\n\nTwo candidate contributors, both worth checking before assuming:\n\n1. **The deployed build may predate the fix.** Commit `7be0edb7132d` (\"re-clone an unusable\n   tickets store\") suggests exactly this class of wedged store was addressed; the container may\n   be older than it, or the store may have been created before it and never re-cloned.\n2. **Credential/permission asymmetry.** The container pushes with `MCP_TICKETS_PAT` (or its\n   documented fallback to `reviewbot-tickets-pat`), a different identity from the developer's.\n   A rejection that reads as 'fetch first' is not necessarily non-fast-forward — verify what the\n   remote actually returns rather than trusting the message.\n\n## Also present on that store\n\n`fsck` reports `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` naming multiple other environment ids — the signature of a\nre-clone that did not carry over its git-ignored local state (`.env-id`, `.opcert-key`). Op-cert\nattestations signed under those identities verify as `foreign_key` at the claim/close gates and\nmust be re-earned. That may be the same underlying event as the wedged store.\n\n## Impact\n\nSilent data loss on the mandated write path. Nothing surfaces to the caller: the MCP tool reports\nsuccess, and the divergence is only visible by running `fsck` against the container's own store.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The deployed MCP server's tickets store pushes successfully to `origin/tickets`, or\n      recovers by merge the way the CLI store does.\n- [ ] A tracker write that cannot reach the shared store FAILS LOUDLY to the caller rather than\n      returning success — silent stranding is the part that makes this dangerous.\n- [ ] The existing backlog on the container is reconciled without losing events (the store is\n      append-only, so a merge should preserve them — verify rather than assume).\n- [ ] `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` on that store is resolved or explicitly accepted with its consequence\n      for attestations recorded.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE: a comment written through the deployed MCP server is\n      observed on `origin/tickets` from a different machine, with the tool response and the\n      resulting commit recorded here.","id":"b928-3ab6-5985-417b","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["mcp","tracker","data-integrity","deploy"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Deployed MCP server's tickets store cannot push: every tracker write is silently stranded in the container"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787891949367268001,"uuid":"0b273b87-041d-4bb2-a1bc-181827803956"}